PlaceMatch embeds data from these projects. Their licenses apply to that data.

libpostal address dictionaries
  https://github.com/openvenues/libpostal (resources/dictionaries)
  Copyright (c) 2015 libpostal contributors. MIT License.
  Copied to crates/placematch/data/dict/.

Google libaddressinput country metadata
  https://github.com/google/libaddressinput (served from chromium-i18n.appspot.com/ssl-address)
  Copyright Google LLC. Apache License 2.0.
  Copied to crates/placematch/data/aid/.

OpenCage address-formatting configuration
  https://github.com/OpenCageData/address-formatting (conf/state_codes.yaml, conf/country2lang.yaml)
  Copyright (c) OpenCage GmbH. MIT License.
  Copied to crates/placematch/data/.

Unicode Han Database (Unihan) readings
  https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/ (Unihan_Readings.txt: kMandarin, kHanyuPinyin,
  kJapaneseOn, kJapaneseKun)
  Copyright (c) 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc. Unicode License v3; see LICENSE-UNICODE.
  Reduced by tools/vendor-readings.py to crates/placematch/data/readings/han.txt.

Wikidata city names
  https://www.wikidata.org (labels of cities of 150,000 people or more)
  Released into the public domain under CC0 1.0.
  Reduced by tools/vendor-exonyms.py to crates/placematch/data/extra/exonyms-wikidata.txt.

The benchmark generator in bench/real/ downloads, but does not redistribute, data from
OpenStreetMap (ODbL 1.0, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors), Overture Maps addresses and
divisions (each record carries its source license; the generator keeps open licenses
only), and the Hugging Face dataset ziozzang/korean_address_en-ko (MIT).
